{"id": "EUVD-2026-97013", "enisaUuid": "5692c25e-fcc0-3e79-b2a5-1c3e69800eb1", "description": "APIPark through 1.9.7-beta contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read other applications' credentials by supplying a foreign authorization UUID. Attackers with authorization-view permission on one application can query /api/v1/app/authorization or its details route to retrieve plaintext API keys regardless of HideCredential.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T13:26:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:59:29", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/apipark-cross-app-authorization-uuid", "https://github.com/APIParkLab/APIPark/blob/v1.9.7-beta/module/application-authorization/iml.go#L451-L511", "https://github.com/APIParkLab/APIPark", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/apipark-through-1.9.7-beta-idor-via-application-authorization-endpoints"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108862", "GHSA-5xgx-36cx-7963"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "48abde98-0719-38ac-b59f-f86320d7cba0", "product": {"name": "APIPark", "vendor": {"name": "APIParkLab"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.9.7-beta"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "78e88803-ceb0-313a-8c38-e7f834006415", "vendor": {"name": "APIParkLab"}}], "isExploited": false}